sequenceDiagram
    autonumber off
    actor Steward
    participant Site as Site page<br/>/detail/[namesite]
    participant Presign as GPX presign route<br/>(Proposed)
    participant S3 as AWS S3
    participant Save as Server action<br/>saveGpxTrack<br/>(Proposed)
    participant DB as Supabase<br/>PostgreSQL

    Note over Steward,DB: Covers US 2.0.9. No GPX upload exists in the code. All steps are Proposed. The flow copies the image upload<br/>pattern: /api/s3/presign-homepage-images, a direct PUT to S3, then a database row (insertHomepageImageUpload).<br/>Storage is not decided. This diagram shows the minimal option: the GPX file in S3 and one track row in the database.

    Steward->>Site: Choose a file and select Upload
    activate Site
    Site->>Site: Check the file extension and size
    alt Extension is not .gpx (AT2)
        Site-->>Steward: Show "Only GPX files are accepted"
    else File is larger than the maximum (AT5)
        Site-->>Steward: Show a refusal that names the size limit
    else Extension and size are correct
        Site->>Presign: POST siteId, file name, file size
        activate Presign
        Presign->>Presign: getUser() and check approved account on server
        alt No session or account not approved
            Presign-->>Site: Refuse (401)
            Site-->>Steward: Go to /login
        else Extension or size is wrong (server check)
            Presign-->>Site: Refuse (400) with the size limit
            Site-->>Steward: Show the refusal
        else Request is correct
            Presign->>S3: Create a presigned PUT URL for a new key
            S3-->>Presign: Upload URL
            Presign-->>Site: Upload URL and storage key
            deactivate Presign
            Site->>S3: PUT the GPX file
            alt Upload fails
                S3-->>Site: Error
                Site-->>Steward: Show "Upload failed, try again". Nothing is saved.
            else Upload done
                S3-->>Site: OK
                Site->>Save: saveGpxTrack(siteId, storageKey)
                activate Save
                Save->>Save: Check session. Take the user id from the session, not from the client.
                Save->>S3: Get the uploaded file
                S3-->>Save: GPX file
                Save->>Save: Parse the GPX and count the track points (AT3)
                alt Not valid GPX or no track points
                    Save->>S3: Delete the uploaded file
                    Save-->>Site: Refuse (422)
                    Site-->>Steward: Show "Not a valid GPX track". Nothing is saved.
                else Valid track
                    Save->>DB: Insert gpx_tracks row: site_id, user_id,<br/>storage key, point count (AT1)
                    activate DB
                    alt Insert fails
                        DB-->>Save: Error
                        Save->>S3: Delete the uploaded file
                        Save-->>Site: Error (500)
                        Site-->>Steward: Show the error. Nothing is saved.
                    else Insert done
                        DB-->>Save: Track id
                        Save-->>Site: Track saved
                        Site-->>Steward: Show "Track saved". The map can draw it (US 2.0.1 AT2).
                    end
                    deactivate DB
                end
                deactivate Save
            end
        end
    end
    deactivate Site

    Note over Steward,DB: The file is stored without change, so a read-back gives the same track points (AT4).<br/>Open questions: where tracks are stored (S3 file or points in the database), the maximum file size,<br/>and whether a Steward can also upload from inside a SIR.<br/>Open question: if the delete of an invalid or unsaved file fails, the file stays in S3. AT 3 says nothing is saved.
